  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that single-profile multimodal PCA+ResNet with concat fusion outperforms RNA-only and image-only models, with weighted fusion only slightly worse. The key uncertainty is whether multiprofile representation plus aggregation can improve on this promising multimodal baseline. config_018 is the best next experiment because it makes the minimal logical extension: it keeps the best-supported encoders and concat fusion while testing multiprofile with a simple avgpool aggregation, helping isolate the effect of profile setting/aggregation before trying more complex transformer aggregation or other encoders."
